            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5",
            "treatment.6"
          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM (laboratory glucose 34), ketones 5.2, pH 7.18 and bicarbonate 11, consistent with severe DKA. PICU was informed and she was managed on ward HDU. The DKA protocol was initiated with cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement and hourly monitoring. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 and ketones to 0.8; she was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. The diabetes nurse and dietician provided input during the admission, and structured education covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management and sick-day rules was delivered. Both parents and the child were confident with injections and monitoring prior to discharge.",
